WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.111
Maya wants to learn whether a small
pollinator garden might

00:00:04.111 --> 00:00:08.042
work at school. She needs permission and
a spot with

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:08.828
suitable light.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.531
First ask a staff sponsor about
permission. Next sketch one

00:00:13.531 --> 00:00:17.882
possible bed and note the sunlight. Then
review the plan

00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:21.362
with the sponsor and decide whether to
continue.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.053
Maya can sketch and observe without
planting. If she cannot

00:00:26.053 --> 00:00:30.326
visit the site safely, she can document
that barrier and

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:33.318
ask what information the sponsor can
share.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.674
A dated sketch or a short note about the
sunlight

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:41.567
could help compare locations. One
observation cannot prove that a

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:44.293
garden will thrive across a whole
season.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.215
Feedback might lead Maya to choose
another spot or gather

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:53.651
more evidence. For your project, name
one safe action, one

00:00:53.651 --> 00:00:57.643
useful observation, and one thing it
would not prove.

